  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 237 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nMonday through Friday:\n\n500 mb cluster analysis generally shows an anomalous 500 mb\nridge developing somewhere over the Upper Midwest or Western\nGreat Lakes regions by the middle to later portions of next\nweek. This should allow for the surface high to gradually shift\neast northeast of the region during this period, keeping\ngenerally southerly winds over the area. This should result in\nsteady warming of temperatures during the week, with ensemble\nmembers supporting highs well into the 60s to around 70 degrees\nby Tuesday and Wednesday, perhaps into the lower 70s inland \nThursday into Friday. Ensemble members also show a dry period \nfor most of the week.\n\nWood",
